<% layout('layout/boilerplate.ejs') %>

<main>
  <section class="section container">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">&larr; Back</a>

    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-card-header">
        <span class="feature-card-dot"></span>
        <span class="feature-card-dot"></span>
        <span class="feature-card-dot"></span>
        <span class="title">free — voult.dev</span>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card-body">
        <div class="feature-full">
          <h1>Free at launch</h1>
          <p class="feature-full-intro">
            We believe developers should be able to build and ship authentication without a procurement process, a sales call, or a credit card form. Here's what "free" actually means on voult.dev.
          </p>

          <h2>What's included</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Every MVP feature, free</strong> — email/password auth, OAuth, magic links, JWT rotation, rate limiting, the dashboard, and the UI kits. None of it is behind a paywall.</li>
            <li><strong>No credit card required</strong> — sign up and start building. We won't ask for payment details until you explicitly upgrade.</li>
            <li><strong>No trial timer counting down</strong> — use the MVP for as long as you need. Evaluate it on your own schedule.</li>
            <li><strong>Generous free tier after launch</strong> — paid plans with higher limits and advanced features will come later. There will always be a free tier for small projects, side projects, and experimentation.</li>
            <li><strong>Fair usage limits</strong> — free tier limits are designed so individuals and small teams can operate normally. We'll publish exact numbers before launch.</li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            Our business model depends on teams scaling up with us, not on trapping small developers behind a paywall.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
